\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{A stabilizer acts on one block of fields}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{A shift multiplies a Fourier mode by a scalar. A coordinate change
permuting its multipliers carries the entire mode to another block.
Several coordinate changes can reach the same [momentum
label](fdip-0164). How much information about all the blocks in one
orbit is already present in the action at just one of them?}

\p{On an axis of a grid, a rotation in a transverse plane can fix the
momentum while acting on the field components. How can its eigenvalues
distinguish components in the same momentum block?}

